    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s original name was Winwood, and early settlers in 1817 included David Wooley, James Moore, and Franklin Duval.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lakewood_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lakewood sits at 1,778 feet above sea level, a height that gives it a cooler climate and occasional lake‑effect snow in winter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
